Pari-veṣṭṛ in the Atharvaveda^1 and later^2 denotes an
‘attendant,’ more especially one who serves up food, a ‘waiter.’
The feminine form Pariveṣṭrī signifies a ‘female attendant’ or
‘handmaid.’^3
